From 8c3e23ec5b9876611c151df85722cc4fc9a5a75f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:45:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] Round 3: Build the lane kernel for AVX2 and widen
 groups to eight lanes

Compile the lockstep lane kernel a second time with the avx2 target
feature and select it at preparation when the host supports AVX2.
AVX2 does not enable fused multiply-add and Rust does not contract
operations, so every lane performs the same IEEE operations; records
stay byte-identical. Widen domain::LANES from four to eight so the
256-bit kernel has enough independent chains to cover the RK4 step
latency. A domain unit test compares the AVX2 and baseline kernels bit
for bit on PD and held models, and the lockstep test now covers batch
sizes up to eleven and ten.

Workload: domain2 (48 full records, held actuation, 4,000 RK4 steps
each, one worker).
Before median: 1.810 ms. After median: 0.995 ms. Speedup: 1.82x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
